  "aboutUs": {
    "title": "About us",
    "about": [
      {
        "title": "What is the Gerege? — Our Historical Foundation",
        "description": "During the time of the Mongol Empire, the “Gerege” was a diplomatic passport issued to emissaries and envoys. It granted them safe passage, food, horses, lodging, and guides across the vast territory of the empire. It was the world’s first form of a universal travel token—unparalleled in any other civilization, even the Roman Empire. The holder of a Gerege traveled freely and received honorable hospitality, symbolizing power, trust, and international authority."
      },
      {
        "title": "Modern Rebirth – The Gerege Tourist Passport",
        "description": "The Gerege Tourist Passport is a contemporary version of this historical legacy—reimagined for today’s travelers. Designed to promote Mongolia’s culture and history to international tourists, it combines educational value with real-world benefits: free access to 8 services, discounts at over 100 partner businesses, and contributions to charitable causes such as children’s welfare."
      },
      {
        "title": "Safe, Simple, Smart, and Saving – The Four Pillars of the Gerege Tourist Passport",
        "description": "These four keywords represent the core strengths of the Gerege Tourist Passport: <br></br> <ul><li><b>Safe:</b> Officially registered and secure, your personal data is protected. The passport supports responsible and safe travel across Mongolia.</li><li><b>Simple:</b> Easy to purchase, use, and redeem discounts. The experience is user-friendly and convenient for all travelers.</li><li><b>Smart:</b> Enhanced with technology—QR codes, an online network of partners, and seamless integration to make your journey efficient and smooth.</li><li><b>Saving:</b> Access discounts at over 100 establishments including hotels, restaurants, and attractions—helping you reduce travel costs without sacrificing quality.</li></ul><br/>The Gerege Tourist Passport is your trusted companion—bridging ancient Mongolian legacy with modern-day travel in a way that is educational, valuable, and inspiring."
      }
    ],

    "benefits": ["Safe", "Simple", "Smart", "Saving"]
  },

